368
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:06,080
- Go for it! Dive in!
- Here we go!

369
00:24:07,240 --> 00:24:09,600
Dive in now.

370
00:24:22,720 --> 00:24:23,920
Dammit!

371
00:24:39,800 --> 00:24:40,800
Jeez.

372
00:24:51,760 --> 00:24:53,400
F♪ck, what the hell was that play?

373
00:24:53,560 --> 00:24:55,800
We did it, Soh! We actually did it!

374
00:24:56,720 --> 00:24:57,640
B.S. Brothers!

375
00:24:57,680 --> 00:25:05,520
- B.S. Brothers! B.S. Brothers!
- B.S. Brothers! B.S. Brothers!

376
00:25:05,640 --> 00:25:06,720
That means...

377
00:25:06,840 --> 00:25:08,840
B.S. Brothers, - B.S. Brothers,

378
00:25:08,880 --> 00:25:11,920
- you are the APL 2026 Champions!
- You are the APL 2026 Champions!

379
00:25:12,480 --> 00:25:15,000
♪ Birthday but with me ♪

380
00:25:15,040 --> 00:25:17,720
(B.S. Brothers!)

381
00:25:18,840 --> 00:25:20,240
(Congratulations!)

382
00:25:21,200 --> 00:25:22,120
(Incredible!)

383
00:25:22,160 --> 00:25:24,520
♪ Could it be I'm missing you? ♪

384
00:25:26,760 --> 00:25:28,600
Look at this! Check it out!

385
00:25:32,720 --> 00:25:33,880
Let me try!

386
00:25:33,920 --> 00:25:37,480
♪ The more it happens, the more I see ♪

387
00:25:38,280 --> 00:25:40,480
♪ Yeah, it must be ♪

388
00:25:43,360 --> 00:25:44,320
Go for it, Jack!

389
00:25:44,360 --> 00:25:46,600
Man, I'm on fire!

390
00:25:50,520 --> 00:25:51,680
Your turn!

391
00:25:52,640 --> 00:25:53,640
One, two...

392
00:25:58,680 --> 00:26:00,000
- Do it!
- Go, P'Toobtub!

393
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:15,360
(The player who stepped in when the team needed them most)

394
00:26:15,640 --> 00:26:19,400
(and perfectly shifted the momentum of the game, )

395
00:26:19,880 --> 00:26:24,600
or the FMVP of this tournament, is...

396
00:26:30,240 --> 00:26:31,536
The FMVP is...

397
00:26:31,560 --> 00:26:33,320
- It's you, P'Three.
- Derya!

398
00:26:41,000 --> 00:26:42,280
MVP!

399
00:26:42,360 --> 00:26:46,360
- MVP!
- MVP!

400
00:26:47,960 --> 00:26:49,480
Hey, give us a smile.

401
00:26:50,680 --> 00:26:52,480
You deserve this more than anyone.

402
00:26:52,600 --> 00:26:54,040
Not just on this stage,

403
00:26:54,240 --> 00:26:55,880
but from the moment you joined our team,

404
00:26:56,120 --> 00:26:57,760
and entered my life,

405
00:26:59,000 --> 00:27:00,480
you've been my MVP.

406
00:27:01,360 --> 00:27:03,200
You've been my MVP, too.

407
00:27:05,360 --> 00:27:08,000
- Someone's so in love here.
- Is it time yet?

408
00:27:08,200 --> 00:27:09,160
- Ready?
- Go for it!

409
00:27:09,200 --> 00:27:11,400
- Alright, group photo!
- Yeah, come on!

410
00:27:11,440 --> 00:27:13,120
- Jeez, what's with you?
- Get in the shot!

411
00:27:13,240 --> 00:27:15,080
Jeez.

412
00:27:15,560 --> 00:27:17,680
Where's the camera? Bring it here!

413
00:27:18,040 --> 00:27:19,656
One, two, three!

414
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:22,720
- B.S. Brothers!
- B.S. Brothers!

415
00:27:39,960 --> 00:27:41,640
And we actually made it happen.

416
00:27:48,920 --> 00:27:50,240
I never imagined

417
00:27:50,920 --> 00:27:53,920
that I would actually win this FMVP award.

418
00:27:54,680 --> 00:27:56,520
I honestly thought P'Three would get it.

419
00:27:58,560 --> 00:28:00,840
Anyway, thank you, everyone,

420
00:28:01,440 --> 00:28:04,280
for always supporting me.

421
00:28:04,960 --> 00:28:06,600
At first, I thought.

422
00:28:07,520 --> 00:28:10,040
I'd only be taking this FMVP trophy home.

423
00:28:10,680 --> 00:28:12,240
But actually, it's much more than that.

424
00:28:13,040 --> 00:28:14,040
Right now,

425
00:28:14,760 --> 00:28:17,640
RoV has given me the opportunity to design a skin.

426
00:28:19,640 --> 00:28:22,280
That's my biggest problem

427
00:28:22,760 --> 00:28:23,640
because I still have no idea

428
00:28:23,680 --> 00:28:26,680
how I'm going to design my own skin.

429
00:28:29,480 --> 00:28:31,560
If it's not too much trouble, could you help me out?

430
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:39,680
If you have any ideas, please let me know.

431
00:28:47,880 --> 00:28:50,120
Derya,

432
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:52,600
your babe is home!

433
00:28:53,080 --> 00:28:55,120
I've been gone all day. So exhausted.

434
00:29:00,200 --> 00:29:01,920
Whoa, what's all this?

435
00:29:06,520 --> 00:29:08,920
A strict art professor wouldn't approve of this.

436
00:29:09,680 --> 00:29:10,680
Soh?

437
00:29:11,960 --> 00:29:13,000
Where are you?

438
00:29:16,080 --> 00:29:16,840
Soh!

439
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:18,600
- P'Three...
- Whoa!

440
00:29:19,280 --> 00:29:21,360
Soh, where are you?

441
00:29:21,840 --> 00:29:23,160
P'Three...

442
00:29:24,760 --> 00:29:26,640
P'Three...

443
00:29:29,160 --> 00:29:30,560
A ghost!

444
00:29:32,160 --> 00:29:33,680
Soh, Soh!

445
00:29:39,600 --> 00:29:42,216
How could I not be startled?

446
00:29:42,240 --> 00:29:45,000
I just finished watching 'After Dark' on WeTV.

447
00:29:45,120 --> 00:29:47,000
Man, no wonder I was creep ed out.

448
00:29:47,560 --> 00:29:48,840
Come on, P'Three.

449
00:29:49,280 --> 00:29:51,800
Did I really look that much like a ghost?

450
00:29:52,880 --> 00:29:54,280
Don't be silly.

451
00:29:58,000 --> 00:29:59,880
Even if you were a ghost,

452
00:29:59,920 --> 00:30:01,880
you'd be my only boo.

453
00:30:02,360 --> 00:30:04,280
You know, my one and only boo.

454
00:30:05,040 --> 00:30:05,720
Stop right there.

455
00:30:05,760 --> 00:30:08,320
I heard someone screamed really loud just now.

456
00:30:10,320 --> 00:30:11,320
Wonder who that could be.

457
00:30:12,960 --> 00:30:14,200
I'm sorry.

458
00:30:14,400 --> 00:30:17,160
I only went home to help out for a little bit.

459
00:30:17,240 --> 00:30:20,440
Now that I'm back, why is my boyfriend like this?

460
00:30:20,840 --> 00:30:23,480
I left you alone for just a second.

461
00:30:23,640 --> 00:30:26,320
Whoa, I really can't let you out of my sight.

462
00:30:27,360 --> 00:30:28,360
Soh,

463
00:30:28,800 --> 00:30:30,720
you need to take care of yourself, okay?

464
00:30:31,440 --> 00:30:33,240
You're the only one for me in this world.

465
00:30:36,080 --> 00:30:37,080
So.

466
00:30:38,400 --> 00:30:40,480
Can I ask you for a favor?

467
00:30:40,520 --> 00:30:42,776
Of course. Whatever you want me to do,

468
00:30:42,800 --> 00:30:44,400
just name it. I'll do anything for you.

469
00:30:50,040 --> 00:30:54,200
Then, could you help me design the skin?

470
00:30:55,520 --> 00:30:58,680
Oh, come on, is that all? I've totally got this.

471
00:30:58,800 --> 00:30:59,920
Did that hurt?

472
00:30:59,960 --> 00:31:01,240
It didn't.

473
00:31:01,440 --> 00:31:02,440
Okay...

474
00:31:04,680 --> 00:31:06,800
It's not quite 100% done.

475
00:31:09,920 --> 00:31:12,240
Why is designing a skin so damn hard?

476
00:31:16,720 --> 00:31:19,456
But out of all of these, I really like this one.

477
00:31:19,480 --> 00:31:21,216
This one, the lion skin.

478
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:24,120
It looks like a fierce, imposing predator, like...

479
00:31:25,200 --> 00:31:26,360
That's a cat.

480
00:31:30,680 --> 00:31:33,440
Do you have your favorite one yet?

481
00:31:37,960 --> 00:31:39,400
It's okay.

482
00:31:39,800 --> 00:31:41,880
We'll keep trying, okay?

483
00:31:44,400 --> 00:31:47,560
What do you want people to see in this skin?

484
00:31:50,080 --> 00:31:51,400
I don't really know.

485
00:31:54,000 --> 00:31:57,560
Maybe a side of me that others haven't seen before.

486
00:31:58,240 --> 00:31:59,480
A side of you?

487
00:32:01,480 --> 00:32:04,360
People usually see me as a derpy kid,

488
00:32:04,400 --> 00:32:05,400
a nerd,

489
00:32:05,680 --> 00:32:06,680
or just a plain guy.

490
00:32:08,160 --> 00:32:10,120
I just want to explore a new side of me,

491
00:32:10,720 --> 00:32:14,320
in case it works for the skin.

492
00:32:18,320 --> 00:32:20,360
Don't you worry, Derpy Kid.

493
00:32:20,720 --> 00:32:23,960
I'm going to help you find that side.

494
00:32:28,920 --> 00:32:29,920
Come on.

495
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:33,000
Let's find your ultimate skin, baby.

496
00:32:40,680 --> 00:32:42,880
I think you need to try something new.

497
00:32:51,160 --> 00:32:52,160
A Luk Thung singer?

498
00:32:52,240 --> 00:32:55,280
Exactly. This is something totally different for you.

499
00:32:55,320 --> 00:32:56,640
Luk Thung music

500
00:32:56,680 --> 00:33:01,200
will definitely reveal another side of you for sure.

501
00:33:01,440 --> 00:33:03,200
Trust me, Derpy Kid.

502
00:33:03,240 --> 00:33:04,776
♪ Alright, baby? ♪

503
00:33:04,800 --> 00:33:06,800
- ♪Alright, baby? ♪
- ♪Alright, baby? ♪

504
00:33:17,360 --> 00:33:18,360
Gosh!

505
00:33:19,160 --> 00:33:20,160
P'Three!

506
00:33:20,520 --> 00:33:21,936
- What?
- Is this my new side,

507
00:33:21,960 --> 00:33:23,800
or is it actually yours?

508
00:33:23,840 --> 00:33:25,040
Since Luk Thung didn't work,

509
00:33:25,200 --> 00:33:26,680
I think you need a spiritual retreat.

510
00:33:27,360 --> 00:33:28,360
Alright.

511
00:33:30,560 --> 00:33:32,800
Master Three.

512
00:33:36,120 --> 00:33:37,280
I think

513
00:33:37,560 --> 00:33:39,120
that one was a bit too chaotic.

514
00:33:39,800 --> 00:33:40,816
For you,

515
00:33:40,840 --> 00:33:44,160
something quiet and peaceful might be better.

516
00:33:47,200 --> 00:33:48,720
Let's meditate.

517
00:33:52,200 --> 00:33:53,280
A peaceful mind

518
00:33:54,080 --> 00:33:55,880
brings clarity.

519
00:33:56,240 --> 00:33:57,320
When there's clarity,

520
00:33:57,760 --> 00:33:59,520
the answers reveal themselves.

521
00:34:05,480 --> 00:34:06,920
Jeez, P'Three.

522
00:34:07,880 --> 00:34:09,976
I think this is too peaceful.

523
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:12,000
- And I'm itchy.
- It's not working?

524
00:34:12,360 --> 00:34:13,440
I don't think it is.

525
00:34:13,480 --> 00:34:14,880
Then let's try something else.

526
00:34:15,160 --> 00:34:16,200
Let's try something else.

527
00:34:18,280 --> 00:34:19,560
Hey, Soh!

528
00:34:21,840 --> 00:34:22,640
What's going on here?

529
00:34:22,680 --> 00:34:24,280
Trouble finds me every time.

530
00:34:24,440 --> 00:34:25,760
Scientists have said that

531
00:34:25,800 --> 00:34:27,960
if we're in a thrilling situation,

532
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,256
the adrenaline will start flowing

533
00:34:29,280 --> 00:34:31,200
and help us discover our hidden skills.

534
00:34:32,400 --> 00:34:33,377
How are you doing?

535
00:34:33,401 --> 00:34:34,656
Found any new sides of yourself?

536
00:34:34,680 --> 00:34:36,040
Isn't this a bit too thrilling?

537
00:34:36,960 --> 00:34:37,960
What now?

538
00:34:42,600 --> 00:34:44,360
How's it going? Any new ideas?

539
00:34:45,520 --> 00:34:47,776
My ideas were blown away by that first explosion.

540
00:34:47,800 --> 00:34:49,640
Jeez, really? Nothing at all?

541
00:34:55,720 --> 00:34:56,896
Listen, Derpy Kid.

542
00:34:56,920 --> 00:34:59,000
I think we should try a film noir vibe.

543
00:34:59,040 --> 00:35:00,696
Whoa, I think this is better.

544
00:35:00,720 --> 00:35:02,440
- This is the one.
- That's enough, P'Three.

545
00:35:03,240 --> 00:35:04,240
I think

546
00:35:04,360 --> 00:35:06,400
I've explored plenty of new sides now,

547
00:35:08,080 --> 00:35:10,040
but none of them actually felt like me.

548
00:35:10,600 --> 00:35:14,560
Maybe I'm just a plain, ordinary guy

549
00:35:15,760 --> 00:35:17,760
with nothing special.

550
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:21,560
Oh, Soh.

551
00:35:22,280 --> 00:35:23,776
Don't put so much pressure on yourself.

552
00:35:23,800 --> 00:35:25,440
Let's just take our time.

553
00:35:26,040 --> 00:35:27,040
Okay?

554
00:35:30,120 --> 00:35:31,400
No matter what you're like,

555
00:35:31,920 --> 00:35:34,480
you'll always have me as your number one support.

556
00:35:41,800 --> 00:35:43,200
I've got it.

557
00:35:43,680 --> 00:35:45,520
I have one more thing I want you to try.

558
00:35:46,480 --> 00:35:47,480
What is it?

559
00:35:48,440 --> 00:35:49,480
Just a second.

560
00:35:58,080 --> 00:35:59,360
Here.

561
00:36:01,120 --> 00:36:03,560
Wait, that's my bear head.

562
00:36:04,320 --> 00:36:05,720
I thought I'd lost it.

563
00:36:06,880 --> 00:36:10,200
Oh, your fans made this one for you.

564
00:36:10,240 --> 00:36:11,680
- My fans?
- Yeah.

565
00:36:12,360 --> 00:36:13,920
But why did they send it to you?

566
00:36:18,000 --> 00:36:19,560
Look at you, catching on.

567
00:36:19,920 --> 00:36:22,280
I was planning to keep it as a little secret.

568
00:36:22,320 --> 00:36:23,720
I wanted all the credit for myself.

569
00:36:24,440 --> 00:36:25,560
I'll admit it.

570
00:36:25,760 --> 00:36:26,760
This...

571
00:36:27,160 --> 00:36:28,480
Your boyfriend made it himself.

572
00:36:31,760 --> 00:36:34,360
I know how much this means to you.

573
00:36:35,360 --> 00:36:37,360
It's a part of who you are.

574
00:36:37,920 --> 00:36:39,400
I couldn't just let it disappear.

575
00:36:52,640 --> 00:36:53,720
Because

576
00:37:04,160 --> 00:37:06,240
you're already the most important person in my life.

577
00:37:37,520 --> 00:37:45,240
♪ They say the words we cannot say are hidden in songs we play, ♪

578
00:37:45,800 --> 00:37:52,240
♪ So I'm sending you this one, hoping you'll feel the same way ♪

579
00:37:52,880 --> 00:37:56,920
♪ And hear what my heart's been trying to say ♪

580
00:37:56,960 --> 00:38:02,896
♪ It's that smile of yours that gets me every time, ♪

581
00:38:02,920 --> 00:38:10,600
♪ Those eyes and that sweet smile, they make my heart go wild ♪

582
00:38:10,880 --> 00:38:17,920
♪ I'll give you my heart if you ever need someone by your side ♪

583
00:38:17,960 --> 00:38:20,080
♪ (Just give me a sign) ♪

584
00:38:20,560 --> 00:38:24,960
♪ No matter how far, I'll always come to you ♪

585
00:38:25,000 --> 00:38:30,680
♪ I'll fill your heart with love as long as you keep smiling, too ♪

586
00:38:31,240 --> 00:38:35,616
♪ When your tears start to fall, I'll hold you tight ♪

587
00:38:35,640 --> 00:38:41,600
♪ And like a game, no matter how hard, we'll win every fight ♪

588
00:39:29,480 --> 00:39:31,200
It's as cute as the person who designed it.

589
00:39:39,120 --> 00:39:41,760
Hello! Can I interview you guys for a moment?

590
00:39:41,840 --> 00:39:42,537
Of course.

591
00:39:42,561 --> 00:39:45,600
Since you guys are out jogging together like this,

592
00:39:45,640 --> 00:39:46,720
what's your relationship?

593
00:39:49,440 --> 00:39:50,440
We're boyfriends.

594
00:39:55,920 --> 00:39:59,136
♪ I'll find my way into your heart one day, ♪

595
00:39:59,160 --> 00:40:01,720
♪ Getting a little closer every day, ♪

596
00:40:01,760 --> 00:40:04,520
♪ Before you even look my way, ♪

597
00:40:06,160 --> 00:40:09,496
♪ Before you realize I'm here to stay ♪

598
00:40:09,520 --> 00:40:12,760
♪ For now, I'll just keep things brotherly ♪

599
00:40:12,800 --> 00:40:15,200
♪ While caring for you secretly ♪

600
00:40:15,240 --> 00:40:18,400
♪ I'll leave no signs for you to see ♪

601
00:40:19,480 --> 00:40:25,560
♪ Until your heart makes room for me ♪

602
00:40:30,640 --> 00:40:31,640
Alright, then.

603
00:40:31,680 --> 00:40:33,736
- Can I take another photo with you?
- Of course.

604
00:40:33,760 --> 00:40:34,400
Come on.

605
00:40:34,440 --> 00:40:35,760
- Let's do a peace sign?
- Got it.

606
00:40:36,840 --> 00:40:37,840
Now, a heart.

607
00:40:39,960 --> 00:40:41,480
- Okay, thank you!
- Thank you!

608
00:40:45,040 --> 00:40:46,800
Soh is here!

609
00:41:06,800 --> 00:41:08,680
Hello, ma boy.

610
00:41:13,040 --> 00:41:14,040
How...

611
00:41:15,480 --> 00:41:17,240
How do I look, P'Three?

612
00:41:18,600 --> 00:41:20,640
You look exactly like the perfect boyfriend for me.

613
00:41:24,960 --> 00:41:26,000
Are you ready?

614
00:41:28,200 --> 00:41:29,200
- Ready?
- I'm ready.

615
00:41:29,840 --> 00:41:30,856
I'm ready.

616
00:41:30,880 --> 00:41:32,120
- Good.
- Right now,

617
00:41:32,160 --> 00:41:37,000
we are at the launch event for the new skin.

618
00:41:37,680 --> 00:41:38,920
Pardon me.

619
00:41:39,040 --> 00:41:42,360
Soh, can I get a quick interview?

620
00:41:42,440 --> 00:41:43,440
Sure.

621
00:41:44,040 --> 00:41:46,240
Is there anything you'd like to say to your fans?

622
00:41:47,920 --> 00:41:49,880
Hi, I'm Soh.

623
00:41:50,440 --> 00:41:53,800
I'm not sure if you'll like the skin I designed.

624
00:41:54,160 --> 00:41:55,936
What do you think of it? Have you seen it yet?

625
00:41:55,960 --> 00:41:57,936
Oh, the fans are asking

626
00:41:57,960 --> 00:42:01,440
if that's Three over there.

627
00:42:02,360 --> 00:42:05,560
No need to turn away! Look over here, come on.

628
00:42:09,640 --> 00:42:12,416
That's right, it's me, Thr33Gamer, the one and only.

629
00:42:12,440 --> 00:42:14,280
Thanks for still remembering me.

630
00:42:14,960 --> 00:42:19,000
But honestly, I feel like I'm stealing the spotlight.

631
00:42:19,440 --> 00:42:22,640
P'Three actually helped me design the skin.

632
00:42:23,440 --> 00:42:24,920
Without him,

633
00:42:25,480 --> 00:42:27,240
the skin wouldn't have turned out this cute.

634
00:42:28,960 --> 00:42:30,440
The fans are screaming!

635
00:42:30,480 --> 00:42:31,400
But moving on,

636
00:42:31,440 --> 00:42:35,240
we'd love to know the backstory of this skin

637
00:42:35,280 --> 00:42:38,616
that's going on sale in just a few minutes.

638
00:42:38,640 --> 00:42:40,520
Could you explain it to us?

639
00:42:40,640 --> 00:42:41,640
Of course.

640
00:42:43,280 --> 00:42:44,480
For me,

641
00:42:45,120 --> 00:42:47,920
this skin represents memories.

642
00:42:48,880 --> 00:42:51,720
The wonderful memories that P'Three

643
00:42:52,360 --> 00:42:55,200
and everyone else on the team gave to me.

644
00:42:55,600 --> 00:42:58,000
I wanted to pass them on to all of you.

645
00:43:01,520 --> 00:43:03,840
- (Get over here! A weapon, huh?)
- (Bring it on! Come on!)

646
00:43:05,520 --> 00:43:06,680
(No! Stop...)

647
00:43:07,800 --> 00:43:08,920
(Guys, cheers!)

648
00:43:10,240 --> 00:43:11,536
A Support player...

649
00:43:11,560 --> 00:43:12,457
(That was satisfying!)

650
00:43:12,481 --> 00:43:14,736
Makes teammates feel secure, (Soh, I grilled this just for you.)

651
00:43:14,760 --> 00:43:17,336
- knowing they're not fighting alone.
- (Chicken breast is good for you.)

652
00:43:17,360 --> 00:43:18,520
But outside the game,

653
00:43:18,840 --> 00:43:20,600
it's actually my teammates and the fans

654
00:43:20,840 --> 00:43:22,480
who make me feel that way.

655
00:43:27,800 --> 00:43:29,920
(Don't be stressed, Derpy Kid.)

656
00:43:38,640 --> 00:43:40,576
- (Hey, Soh! Put it in!)
- (Let's go!)

657
00:43:40,600 --> 00:43:44,240
(Pluck all this, take the championship!)

658
00:43:45,800 --> 00:43:46,960
(This is the prime tea tip!)

659
00:43:47,120 --> 00:43:49,040
So, from now on,

660
00:43:49,600 --> 00:43:53,600
let this little bear support and fight alongside you.

661
00:43:55,280 --> 00:43:59,040
The fans are ready to hit that buy button now.

662
00:43:59,080 --> 00:44:02,840
Is there anything you'd like to say to the fans?

663
00:44:03,160 --> 00:44:05,280
If you have a soft spot for this little bear, Derya,

664
00:44:06,200 --> 00:44:08,840
then let it support you all

665
00:44:08,880 --> 00:44:10,280
and fight by your side.

666
00:44:11,120 --> 00:44:13,920
Don't forget to top up your vouchers and get your own little bear.

667
00:44:16,040 --> 00:44:18,840
What about you, Three? Anything to say to the fans?

668
00:44:20,560 --> 00:44:22,720
Well, since Soh put it so nicely,

669
00:44:22,920 --> 00:44:25,120
please don't forget to take this Derya bear

670
00:44:25,160 --> 00:44:26,480
to support you in your matches.

671
00:44:26,680 --> 00:44:28,000
However,

672
00:44:28,040 --> 00:44:31,600
don't forget that you can only own the skin

673
00:44:32,120 --> 00:44:35,520
because I'm the real owner of this bear-head gamer's heart.

674
00:44:37,840 --> 00:44:38,880
How exciting!

675
00:44:39,440 --> 00:44:40,880
Give me a second to catch my breath.

676
00:44:41,000 --> 00:44:44,520
All of us here are fans of B.S. Brothers.

677
00:45:07,680 --> 00:45:10,040
(P'Toobtub)

678
00:45:13,200 --> 00:45:13,920
Yes?

679
00:45:13,960 --> 00:45:15,400
(Get to the cafe!)

680
00:45:15,440 --> 00:45:16,240
(Right now!)

681
00:45:16,280 --> 00:45:17,280
What?

682
00:45:21,000 --> 00:45:22,280
Is something wrong?

683
00:45:25,480 --> 00:45:27,440
- Why is it so quiet in here?
- Hey, P'Three! Soh!

684
00:45:28,520 --> 00:45:30,080
How did you guys get here?

685
00:45:30,240 --> 00:45:31,600
All of you are here?

686
00:45:34,560 --> 00:45:36,840
I missed this old vibe.

687
00:45:36,920 --> 00:45:39,040
The smell reminds me of my old home.

688
00:45:39,720 --> 00:45:42,320
Usually, "old home" is code for a grave, you know.

689
00:45:43,760 --> 00:45:44,800
Watch your mouth!

690
00:45:47,000 --> 00:45:48,760
What did we agree on?

691
00:45:50,960 --> 00:45:53,080
Fine, I'll slap my mouth three times.

692
00:45:53,400 --> 00:45:57,080
Look at you. Are you scared of your boyfriend now?

693
00:45:57,480 --> 00:45:58,480
Boyfriend, my ♪ss.

694
00:45:58,520 --> 00:46:00,080
Aw, come on.

695
00:46:01,000 --> 00:46:03,400
- Playing tough, huh?
- Guys, get over here!

696
00:46:03,480 --> 00:46:05,040
Hurry up, come in here.

697
00:46:07,680 --> 00:46:08,680
Come on!

698
00:46:10,920 --> 00:46:12,200
Easy there, sweetie.

699
00:46:12,720 --> 00:46:14,680
Stay calm now, my girl.

700
00:46:15,720 --> 00:46:16,920
Help me out!

701
00:46:17,400 --> 00:46:18,600
I haven't slept a wink.

702
00:46:18,640 --> 00:46:19,680
Tangran

703
00:46:19,800 --> 00:46:22,880
has been crying from midnight till noon.

704
00:46:22,920 --> 00:46:23,760
I haven't had a single break.

705
00:46:23,800 --> 00:46:25,640
Help me babysit her, will you?

706
00:46:26,880 --> 00:46:27,880
Please.

707
00:46:29,680 --> 00:46:31,960
Soh, take her. Alright.

708
00:46:32,840 --> 00:46:33,840
Here, P'Three.

709
00:46:34,080 --> 00:46:35,160
Don't you want to hold her?

710
00:47:15,480 --> 00:47:18,000
- We were throwing hands right here.
- Shut up. Stop talking.

711
00:47:18,040 --> 00:47:19,776
Right, or I'll end up forgetting.

712
00:47:19,800 --> 00:47:23,680
- Yeah, you just keep blabbering on.
- Yeah, you're right.

713
00:47:24,280 --> 00:47:25,976
- Oh, there he is.
- Sit down.

714
00:47:26,000 --> 00:47:27,280
Your hair is a total mess.

715
00:47:27,480 --> 00:47:28,760
I'm beat. So exhausted.

716
00:47:28,800 --> 00:47:31,440
Getting my daughter, Tangran, to go to sleep...

717
00:47:31,480 --> 00:47:33,120
She just wouldn't stop crying.

718
00:47:33,160 --> 00:47:34,720
So is she finally out?

719
00:47:34,800 --> 00:47:36,000
Just drifted off a second ago.

720
00:47:37,960 --> 00:47:40,600
But everything around here has improved so much.

721
00:47:40,960 --> 00:47:42,680
It's nothing like when I used to live here.

722
00:47:44,000 --> 00:47:45,960
I really have to thank you guys

723
00:47:46,040 --> 00:47:48,440
for putting this place on the map.

724
00:47:49,560 --> 00:47:52,120
Whoa, don't mention it. It was a breeze.

725
00:47:52,160 --> 00:47:54,616
Your cafe is basically ours.

726
00:47:54,640 --> 00:47:56,960
Your kid is basically ours.

727
00:47:57,120 --> 00:48:00,200
- And your wife is basically...
- Our mother.

728
00:48:00,240 --> 00:48:01,600
Exactly.

729
00:48:03,200 --> 00:48:04,840
You've got a real big mouth, don't you?

730
00:48:06,040 --> 00:48:08,560
Come to think of it, now that you guys aren't around

731
00:48:08,640 --> 00:48:10,200
I miss you all like crazy.

732
00:48:10,400 --> 00:48:12,120
There's no one for me to annoy anymore.

733
00:48:13,520 --> 00:48:15,080
P'Laem is right.

734
00:48:15,440 --> 00:48:18,080
Ever since APL ended, we haven't really been to the training camp.

735
00:48:18,760 --> 00:48:20,360
It's nice in a way, I guess,

736
00:48:21,120 --> 00:48:23,160
but it's also pretty lonely.

737
00:48:23,200 --> 00:48:24,200
Right.

738
00:48:24,720 --> 00:48:28,880
Ever since my daughter was born, I haven't had a second to rest.

739
00:48:29,280 --> 00:48:31,800
I'm super busy and barely getting any sleep.

740
00:48:34,440 --> 00:48:36,240
Anyway, what are you guys up to these days?

741
00:48:36,920 --> 00:48:38,000
Well.

742
00:48:38,720 --> 00:48:40,840
I'm back to being an office worker again,

743
00:48:41,840 --> 00:48:43,080
but on the bright side,

744
00:48:43,440 --> 00:48:45,000
the office is full of fans now.

745
00:48:45,880 --> 00:48:47,320
Jeez.

746
00:49:02,440 --> 00:49:05,120
You're my bias in B.S. Brothers!

747
00:49:05,240 --> 00:49:06,240
Thanks.

748
00:49:06,840 --> 00:49:08,320
Bye-bye!

749
00:49:11,760 --> 00:49:13,160
And one more thing

750
00:49:13,440 --> 00:49:16,000
I have a new intern I need to train.

751
00:49:16,120 --> 00:49:17,496
You saw me waving at you earlier.

752
00:49:17,520 --> 00:49:19,080
Why didn't you bring me along?

753
00:49:20,920 --> 00:49:22,080
I knew it.

754
00:49:22,120 --> 00:49:23,160
Look at Laem.

755
00:49:23,200 --> 00:49:25,056
He looks like he's been in his final year for three years.

756
00:49:25,080 --> 00:49:26,600
It's the damn company.

757
00:49:26,640 --> 00:49:28,976
They're working me to the bone.

758
00:49:29,000 --> 00:49:32,560
Meeting minutes, coffee runs, photocopying...

759
00:49:32,600 --> 00:49:34,800
Man, they make me do everything.

760
00:49:34,840 --> 00:49:37,480
- It's always just me.
- Just you and you, huh?

761
00:49:37,520 --> 00:49:38,520
You're damn right.

762
00:49:38,600 --> 00:49:40,200
What the hell is this machine?

763
00:49:40,600 --> 00:49:43,320
They keep giving me work I don't know how to do.

764
00:49:43,360 --> 00:49:44,880
Why are there so many buttons?

765
00:49:46,920 --> 00:49:48,240
God,

766
00:49:48,440 --> 00:49:50,560
could you please stop testing me?

767
00:49:50,600 --> 00:49:52,760
Send something good my way for a change.

768
00:49:56,720 --> 00:49:58,240
- Boss?
- For you.

769
00:49:58,280 --> 00:50:00,440
I ordered the wrong thing. I don't like whipped cream.

770
00:50:02,920 --> 00:50:04,936
- Oh, I feel so bad for you.
- Right?

771
00:50:04,960 --> 00:50:06,656
Yeah, I haven't seen you stream live lately.

772
00:50:06,680 --> 00:50:09,440
Come on, you're acting like you'd play with me if I streamed.

773
00:50:09,640 --> 00:50:11,800
You're so famous now, come on.

774
00:50:11,840 --> 00:50:13,936
No way, I'm not that famous.

775
00:50:13,960 --> 00:50:17,080
I'm just the breakout streamer of the year, you know.

776
00:50:19,000 --> 00:50:20,640
That's it for now, everyone.

777
00:50:20,680 --> 00:50:24,480
How was that match? Let me check the comments.

778
00:50:26,040 --> 00:50:28,080
(You look so cute today.)

779
00:50:28,200 --> 00:50:30,280
No way, you're kidding.

780
00:50:30,360 --> 00:50:31,640
Well said! I'll give you twenty.

781
00:50:31,680 --> 00:50:32,680
Wait!

782
00:50:33,120 --> 00:50:35,976
Did TenTen just donate ten thousand?

783
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:37,240
I'm so excited!

784
00:50:37,520 --> 00:50:39,000
Thank you!

785
00:50:39,760 --> 00:50:41,360
Not bad at all.

786
00:50:42,800 --> 00:50:44,720
I think you're more famous than me now.

787
00:50:44,760 --> 00:50:47,440
I could never compare to the great Thr33Gamer.

788
00:50:47,880 --> 00:50:49,880
Just being able to come back makes me so happy.

789
00:50:51,920 --> 00:50:52,960
So, how about you?

790
00:50:53,080 --> 00:50:54,520
Are you staying in Vietnam for long?

791
00:50:54,720 --> 00:50:56,816
Don't forget your old team now that you've got a new one.

792
00:50:56,840 --> 00:50:58,160
You're always so dramatic.

793
00:50:58,320 --> 00:50:59,720
How could I ever forget you guys

794
00:51:00,240 --> 00:51:01,760
when you're all this adorable?

795
00:51:01,800 --> 00:51:04,640
Wait, who's adorable? Tell me!

796
00:51:04,760 --> 00:51:05,800
Everyone, obviously.

797
00:51:06,040 --> 00:51:08,200
- Is that so?
- You sure?

798
00:51:08,360 --> 00:51:09,360
Is that so?

799
00:51:28,400 --> 00:51:29,960
Alright, whatever you say.

800
00:51:30,240 --> 00:51:31,840
Look, guys, I...

801
00:51:32,840 --> 00:51:34,896
- Can I get a hug?
- Whoa, what's with you?

802
00:51:34,920 --> 00:51:36,600
I f♪cking missed you guys.

803
00:51:36,640 --> 00:51:39,400
I don't know when we'll all be together like this again.

804
00:51:39,440 --> 00:51:41,760
Come on, please. Group hug! Come on!

805
00:51:42,320 --> 00:51:43,880
Get up! Hurry!

806
00:51:44,000 --> 00:51:46,640
- Come on, group up!
- Get in here!

807
00:51:48,800 --> 00:51:51,000
Wait, aren't we missing someone?

808
00:51:52,560 --> 00:51:54,040
